+++ b/README.md
@@ -407,6 +407,79 @@ world.onAdd(ChildOf(parent), (entity, target) => {})
 world.onAdd(ChildOf('*'), (entity, target) => {})
 ```
 
+### Aspects
+
+Aspects group two or more traits into a single unit with unified operations. Instead of listing the same traits everywhere and merging their data by hand, define an aspect once and use it anywhere a trait can go.
+
+```js
+import { createAspect, trait } from 'koota'
+
+const Position = trait({ x: 0, y: 0 })
+const Velocity = trait({ dx: 0, dy: 0 })
+
+// An aspect of two or more traits
+const Movement = createAspect(Position, Velocity)
+
+// Aspects expose their id, flattened traits and merged schema
+Movement.traits // [Position, Velocity]
+Movement.schema // { x: 0, y: 0, dx: 0, dy: 0 }
+```
+
+Constituent field names must be unique — overlapping fields throw at creation time, as do relation constituents. Tag traits are valid constituents, and nesting an aspect inside another flattens it into its individual traits.
+
+Entity operations treat the aspect as all of its constituents at once:
+
+```js
+const entity = world.spawn()
+
+// Adds only the constituents the entity is missing, distributing values by field
+entity.add(Movement({ x: 10, dy: 1 }))
+
+// True only when the entity has every constituent
+entity.has(Movement) // true
+
+// Returns a merged object of all constituent fields,
+// or undefined if any constituent is missing
+entity.get(Movement) // { x: 10, y: 0, dx: 0, dy: 1 }
+
+// Distributes each field to its owning constituent with per-trait change detection
+entity.set(Movement, { x: 20, dx: 2 })
+
+// Removes all constituent traits
+entity.remove(Movement)
+```
+
+Used as a query parameter, an aspect requires all of its constituents and delivers one merged data object per entity.
+
+```js
+world.query(Movement).updateEach(([movement]) => {
+  movement.x += movement.dx
+  movement.y += movement.dy
+}) // Writes are distributed back to the constituent stores
+```
+
+Aspects compose with all query modifiers. `Not` matches entities missing at least one constituent. `Added` matches the transition to all-present, `Removed` the transition from all-present, and `Changed` matches when any constituent's data changes while all are present.
+
+```js
+world.query(Not(Movement)) // Missing Position, Velocity or both
+world.query(Added(Movement)) // Just gained the last missing constituent
+world.query(Removed(Movement)) // Just lost a constituent while complete
+world.query(Changed(Movement)) // Position or Velocity data changed
+```
+
+Aspect events fire on completeness transitions:
+
+```js
+// Fires when an entity gains its last missing constituent
+world.onAdd(Movement, (entity) => {})
+
+// Fires when a complete entity loses any constituent
+world.onRemove(Movement, (entity) => {})
+
+// Fires when any constituent changes while all are present
+world.onChange(Movement, (entity) => {})
+```
+
 ### Query modifiers
 
 Modifiers are used to filter query results enabling powerful patterns. All modifiers can be mixed together.
