+---
+title: Aspect
+description: Aspect API
+nav: 8
+---
+
+Aspects group two or more traits into a single unit with unified operations. Anywhere you would list the same traits together and merge their data by hand, an aspect can be used instead.
+
+- [Basic Usage](#Basic-Usage)
+- [Entity operations](#Entity-operations)
+- [Queries](#Queries)
+- [Query modifiers](#Query-modifiers)
+- [Events](#Events)
+
+## Basic Usage
+
+Create an aspect from two or more traits with `createAspect`.
+
+```js
+import { createAspect, trait } from 'koota'
+
+const Position = trait({ x: 0, y: 0 })
+const Velocity = trait({ dx: 0, dy: 0 })
+
+const Movement = createAspect(Position, Velocity)
+```
+
+Each aspect exposes:
+
+```js
+Movement.id // Unique id
+Movement.traits // [Position, Velocity] (flattened)
+Movement.schema // { x: 0, y: 0, dx: 0, dy: 0 } (merged)
+```
+
+Creation rules:
+
+- Constituent field names must be unique. Overlapping fields throw at creation time since writes could not be distributed unambiguously.
+- Relations cannot be constituents and throw at creation time.
+- Tag traits are valid constituents.
+- AoS (callback-based) traits cannot be constituents since their instances cannot be merged.
+- Nesting an aspect flattens it into its individual traits.
+
+```js
+const Actor = createAspect(Movement, Health) // [Position, Velocity, Health]
+```
+
+Every `createAspect` call returns a distinct instance, even for identical constituents.
+
+## Entity operations
+
+Entity and world operations treat an aspect as all of its constituents at once.
+
+```js
+// Adds only the constituents the entity does not already have,
+// distributing initial values to constituents by field.
+entity.add(Movement({ x: 10, dy: 1 }))
+
+// True only when the entity has every constituent trait.
+entity.has(Movement)
+
+// Returns a merged object of all constituent fields,
+// or undefined if any constituent is missing.
+const movement = entity.get(Movement)
+
+// Distributes each field to its owning constituent and
+// triggers change detection per constituent trait.
+entity.set(Movement, { x: 20, dx: 2 })
+entity.set(Movement, (prev) => ({ x: prev.x + prev.dx }))
+
+// Removes all constituent traits.
+entity.remove(Movement)
+```
+
+## Queries
+
+Used as a query parameter, an aspect requires all of its constituents. `readEach` and `updateEach` deliver a single merged data object per entity, and `updateEach` distributes writes back to the constituent stores with per-trait change detection.
+
+```js
+world.query(Movement).updateEach(([movement]) => {
+  movement.x += movement.dx
+  movement.y += movement.dy
+})
+```
+
+## Query modifiers
+
+Aspects compose with all query modifiers.
+
+```js
+// Matches entities missing at least one constituent
+world.query(Not(Movement))
+
+// Matches the transition to all-constituents-present
+world.query(Added(Movement))
+
+// Matches the transition from all-constituents-present
+world.query(Removed(Movement))
+
+// Matches when any constituent's data changed while all are present
+world.query(Changed(Movement))
+
+// Matches entities that are complete or have Health
+world.query(Or(Movement, Health))
+```
+
+## Events
+
+Aspect events fire on completeness transitions.
+
+```js
+// Fires when an entity transitions from incomplete to complete
+world.onAdd(Movement, (entity) => {})
+
+// Fires when an entity transitions from complete to incomplete
+world.onRemove(Movement, (entity) => {})
+
+// Fires when any constituent changes while all are present
+world.onChange(Movement, (entity) => {})
+```
